# Node security group egress (terraform-aws-modules/eks/aws/node_groups.tf,
# resource "egress_all"): worker nodes need broad outbound access to pull
# container images from ECR/DockerHub, reach the EKS/STS/ECR APIs, and
# resolve DNS. Properly restricting this requires VPC endpoints for every
# AWS service the nodes call plus a registry IP allowlist -- accepted as a
# known risk for this cluster rather than undertaken here.
AWS-0104

# EKS API endpoint (terraform-aws-modules/eks/aws): this rule wants the
# endpoint fully private (no public CIDR at all), which would require a
# VPN/bastion host to reach it -- out of scope for this cluster. We already
# restrict cluster_endpoint_public_access_cidrs to a single operator /32
# (see environments/*/terraform.tfvars) instead of leaving it at the
# module's 0.0.0.0/0 default; the rule still flags any public CIDR, however
# narrow.
AWS-0040
AWS-0041
